  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 36,
    "summary": "Elihu says, Those who are righteous are prospered—The wicked perish and die without knowledge—Elihu praises the greatness of God.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Elihu also proceeded, and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Suffer me a little, and I will shew thee that I have yet to speak on God’s behalf.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "I will fetch my knowledge from afar, and will ascribe righteousness to my Maker.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "For truly my words shall not be false: he that is perfect in knowledge is with thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, God is mighty, and despiseth not any: he is mighty in strength and wisdom.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Hate."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG God, Wisdom of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 51
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Hate.",
            "prettyString": "TG Hate",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Hate",
                "entryId": "tg-hate",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "TG God, Wisdom of.",
            "prettyString": "TG God, Wisdom of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "God, Wisdom of",
                "entryId": "tg-god-wisdom-of",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "He preserveth not the life of the wicked: but giveth right to the poor.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "He withdraweth not his eyes from the righteous: but with kings are they on the throne; yea, he doth establish them for ever, and they are exalted.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And if they be bound in fetters, and be holden in cords of affliction;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Then he sheweth them their work, and their transgressions that they have exceeded.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "He openeth also their ear to discipline, and commandeth that they return from iniquity.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "If they obey and serve him, they shall spend their days in prosperity, and their years in pleasures.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Probation."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "HEB pleasantness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Probation.",
            "prettyString": "TG Probation",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Probation",
                "entryId": "tg-probation",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "But if they obey not, they shall perish by the sword, and they shall die without knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Disobedience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Disobedience.",
            "prettyString": "TG Disobedience",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Disobedience",
                "entryId": "tg-disobedience",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "But the hypocrites in heart heap up wrath: they cry not when he bindeth them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "They die in youth, and their life is among the unclean.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "He delivereth the poor in his affliction, and openeth their ears in oppression.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Deliver."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Deliver.",
            "prettyString": "TG Deliver",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Deliver",
                "entryId": "tg-deliver",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Even so would he have removed thee out of the strait into a broad place, where there is no straitness; and that which should be set on thy table should be full of fatness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 87
          },
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 154
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "But thou hast fulfilled the judgment of the wicked: judgment and justice take hold on thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 91
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Because there is wrath, beware lest he take thee away with his stroke: then a great ransom cannot deliver thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Will he esteem thy riches? no, not gold, nor all the forces of strength.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Desire not the night, when people are cut off in their place.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Take heed, regard not iniquity: for this hast thou chosen rather than affliction.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, God exalteth by his power: who teacheth like him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Who hath enjoined him his way? or who can say, Thou hast wrought iniquity?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Remember that thou magnify his work, which men behold.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "Every man may see it; man may behold it afar off.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, God is great, and we know him not, neither can the number of his years be searched out.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "For he maketh small the drops of water: they pour down rain according to the vapour thereof:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "Which the clouds do drop and distil upon man abundantly.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Also can any understand the spreadings of the clouds, or the noise of his tabernacle?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, he spreadeth his light upon it, and covereth the bottom of the sea.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "For by them judgeth he the people; he giveth meat in abundance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "With clouds he covereth the light; and commandeth it not to shine by the cloud that cometh betwixt.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 65
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:32",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "The noise thereof sheweth concerning it, the cattle also concerning the vapour.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 36:33",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 36,
        "verse": 33
      }
    ]
  },
